rivers
shape
the
land
around
them
.
over
thousands
of
years
,
they
carve
valleys
and
build
up
plains
.
when
a
river
floods
,
it
leaves
behind
fine
silt
.
farmers
have
relied
on
that
silt
for
as
long
as
there
have
been
farms
.
the
nile
is
the
best
known
example
.
today
many
rivers
are
held
back
by
dams
.
that
brings
power
and
water
,
but
it
also
stops
the
